          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %em heap
            is an algebraic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            which is almost that of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            structure but without the specification of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
          %p
            While closely related to notions such as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+homogeneous+space"} principal homogeneous space
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ternary"} ternary
            operation obeying two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            (see Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheDefinition"}
            below).
          %p
            Concretely, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            gives a heap where this ternary operation is defined from the group’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mtext -
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mtext -
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\text{-})\cdot(\text{-})
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inversion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1}
            by
          #eq:HeapOperationInAGroup.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  t
                  \\,\colon\,
                  (a,b,c)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  a \cdot b^{-1} \cdot c
          %p
            and every heap arises this way, up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            (cf. Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrinIsEssentiallySurjective"}
            below) from a group that may be called its
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
          %p
            However, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of heaps (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfHeaps"}
            below) is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} category of groups
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %br>/
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of heaps (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfHeaps"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the evident category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              consisting of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and a
              = succeed "-torsor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              On the one hand, for any heap
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h' \in H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctions"} endofunctions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(h,h',-) \colon H \to H
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in H
              constitute a group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              under
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              of the heap manifestly carries the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of a
              = succeed "-torsor." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and a
              = succeed "-torsor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              we can make
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              into a heap as follows: given elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c \in H
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,c) = g c
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is the unique
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g b = a
          %p
            There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            version of the concept of heap, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+heap"} quantum heap
          %p
          #Disambiguation.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (disambiguation)
              %br/
              Heaps in the sense of algebra should not be confused with either
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heap"} heaps
                in the sense of theoretical
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
            %p nor with
            %ul
              %li
                %em heaps of pieces
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorial
                sense of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/BFb0072524"} Viennot 2006
            %p
          %p
          #Synonyms.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (synonyms)
              %br/
              There are also a number of synonyms for the term ‘heap’;
              %a{:href => "#HeapsAndTorsors"} below
              we consider ‘
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"}> torsor
              ’ in this light. In Russian one term for a heap is ‘груда’ (‘gruda’) meaning a heap of soil; this is a pun as it is parallel to the Russian word ‘группа’ (‘gruppa’) meaning a group: forgetting the unit element is sort of creating an amorphous version. This term also appears in English as ‘groud’. In universal algebra the standard name is
              %strong associative Malcev algebra
              (in various spellings, including Mal’cev, Mal’tsev and Maltsev), other names include
              = succeed "." do
                %strong herd
          %p
            There is an oidification (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"}> horizontal categorification
            ) of heaps, sometimes called
            = succeed "." do
              %em heapoids
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #TheDefinition.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong heap
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H,t)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              equipped with a ternary operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi H
                    %mo ×
                    %mi H
                    %mo ×
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \colon H \times H \times H\to H
              satisfying the following two relations
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi c
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(b,b,c) = c = t(c,b,b)
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\big(a,b,t(c,d,e)\big) = t\big(t(a,b,c),d,e\big)
                  \.
            %p
          %p
            More generally, a ternary operation in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety+of+algebras"} variety of algebras
            satisfying the first pair of equations is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcev+operation"} Malcev operation
            %em associative
            if it also satisfies the latter equation (i.e. it makes its domain into a heap).
          %p
            A heap is
            %strong abelian
            if it additionally satisfies the relation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  t(a,b,c) = t(c,b,a)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              A heap always satisfies the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a, t(d, c, b), e) = t(t(a, b, c), d, e)
              (
              %a{:href => "#HollingsLawson"}> Hollings and Lawson 2017
              , theorem 8.2.13).
          %p
          #CategoryOfHeaps.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of heaps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon H \to H'
              is, of course, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              which respects the ternary operations.
            %p
              This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heap
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are heaps and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              are heap homomorphisms.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AbHeap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AbHeap
            of abelian heaps inherit an abelian heap structure from the pointwise operation in the codomain: given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g,h\colon H \to G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\mapsto t_G(f(a),g(a),h(a))
            is again a heap homomorphism.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#StructureGroupsOfHeaps Structure groups of heaps
          %p
            As indicated in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HeapOperationInAGroup"} (1)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            becomes a heap by setting
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a,b,c \,\in\, G
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\vdash
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  t(a,b,c) \,\coloneqq\, a \cdot b^{-1} \cdot c
                  \\,.
          %p
          #PrinIsEssentiallySurjective.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              This construction
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HeapOperationInAGroup"} (1)
              defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prin
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Prin
                    \\,\colon\,
                    Grp \longrightarrow Heap
            %p
              from the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              to that of heaps, which is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              all heaps arise in this way.
            %p In fact, there is also a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Heap
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Str
                    \\,\colon\,
                    Heap \longrightarrow Grp
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there exist
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural
                  group isomorphisms of the form
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi Prin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≅
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str\big(Prin(G)\big) \,\cong\, G
              %li
                %p there exist heap isomorphisms of the form
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Prin
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≅
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prin\big(Str(H)\big) \,\cong\, H
                %p
                  which however are
                  %em not
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
                  (whence we do
                  %em not
                  have an
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            %p
          This group
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mi Str
                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                %mi H
                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
          is called the
          %em structure group
          of the heap
          = succeed "." do
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Given a heap
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
              is described, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Choosing any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e} \in H
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
                #eq:BinaryOperationInFirstModel.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi b
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        a \cdot b \,\coloneqq\, t(a, \mathrm{e} ,b)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  constitutes a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e}
                %p
                  This serves as the required structure group:
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Str
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ≔
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H) \,\coloneqq\, (H, \cdot)
              %li
                %p
                  Take the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  to be that of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi H
                          %mo ×
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b) \in H\times H
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext iff
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (a,b) \,\sim\, (a',b')
                        \\;\;\;\;\text{iff}\;\;\;\;
                        t(a,b,b') \,=\, a'
                %p
                  (the idea is to think of the pair
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
                  as the representative of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b^{-1}
                %p
                  and take the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
                  on the group to be given on representatives by
                #eq:BinaryOperationInSecondModel.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (c,d) \cdot (a,b)
                        \\,\coloneqq\,
                        \\big( c, t(d,a,b) \big)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This again defines a group
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Str
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                %p Notice that:
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inverse
                      of (the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
                      of)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
                      is (the equivalence class of)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,a)
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
                      is (the equivalence class of)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,a)
                      (for any
                      = succeed ")." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi a
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %li
                %p
                  Finally,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  is realized also as an actual
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley%27s+theorem"} Cayley's theorem
                  for groups. We take the elements of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  to be set
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
                  of the form
                #eq:GroupActionInThirdModel.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi H
                        %mo →
                        %mi H
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        t(a,b,-) \,\colon\, H \rightarrow H
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in H
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  as the group’s
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
                %p Notice here that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mrow
                            %mi Str
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        t(c,d,-) \cdot_{Str(H)} t(a,b,-)
                        \\;=\;
                        t\big(c,d,t(a,b,-)\big) \;=\; t\big(t(c,d,a),b,-\big)
                        \\,,
                %p
                  so that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  is closed under this operation.
                %p
                  The first axiom of a heap shows that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  contains the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(-,x,x)
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inverse element
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(\cdot,a,b)
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(\cdot,b,a)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
                  is a subgroup of the symmetric group of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %p It remains to see that these constructions all agree and are functorial.
            %p
              First to show that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              used in the second construction is symmetric, and that it coincides with that implicitly used in the first construction, notice that the following are equivalent:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  (i) the bijections
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,-)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a',b',-)
                  coincide
              %li
                %p
                  (ii)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,b') = a'
              %li
                %p
                  (iii)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a',b',b) = a
            %p Namely:
            %p
              (ii) follows from (i) and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,a,b) = b
            %p
              (ii) implies (iii) as follows. Given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,b') = a'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(t(a,b,b'),b',b) = t(a',b',b)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(t(a,b,b'),b',b) = t(a,b,t(b',b',b)) = t(a,b,b) = a
            %p
              so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a',b',b) = a
            %p (i) follows from (ii) by the calculation:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    t(a',b',x) = t(a',b',t(b,b,x))= t(t(a',b',b),b,x)
                    t(a,b,x)
            %p
              Since the composition laws can also be seen to agree, the second two constructions of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
              are canonically isomorphic.
            %p
              To compare them to the first construction, observe that for a fixed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e} \in H
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{e},a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,c)
              is in the equivalence class, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is determined by
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = t(\mathrm{e},b,c)
            %p Finally, the second construction is manifestly functorial.
          %p
            The following proposition expands on the fact that a group is the same as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed"} pointed
            heap, i.e. a heap with a chosen element:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The category of groups is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow \mathrm{Heap}
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is the terminal heap and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Heap}
              is the category of heaps (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfHeaps"}
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The one-element set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is a heap in a unique way, and for any heap
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: 1 \to H
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: H \to 1
              is a heap homomorphism, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is the terminal object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Heap}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow \mathrm{Heap}
              is the category of pointed heaps. As noted in the proof of the previous proposition, a heap
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              with a chosen point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e}
              becomes a group with multiplication
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi b
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b \,\coloneqq\, t(a, \mathrm{e} ,b)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Grp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow \mathrm{Heap} \to \mathrm{Grp}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Grp
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Grp} \to 1 \downarrow \mathrm{Heap}
              sending any group to the corresponding pointed heap.
          %h3#HeapsAndTorsors Relation to torsors
          %p
            Given a group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            is a nonempty set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a free and transitive action of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi G
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mtd
                        %mo →
                      %mtd
                        %mi X
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mi g
                        %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccl}
                  G \times X &amp;\to&amp; X \\
                  (g, x) &amp;\mapsto&amp; g x
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            Equivalently, a
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} action
            of the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            but also a “division” operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mtd
                        %mo →
                      %mtd
                        %mi G
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccl}
                  X \times X &amp;\to&amp; G \\
                  (x, y) &amp;\mapsto&amp; x/y
                  \\end{array}
          %p obeying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x/y) y = x
          %p
            Given a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            together with a
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into a heap by giving it the ternary operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mtd
                        %mo →
                      %mtd
                        %mi X
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccl}
                  X \times X \times X &amp;\to&amp; X \\
                  (x, y, z) &amp;\mapsto&amp; (x/y) z
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            Conversely, from any heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            we can construct a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            together with a
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            itself. To see this, note that the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Str(H)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PrinIsEssentiallySurjective"} (?)
            comes equipped with a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GroupActionInThirdModel"} (4)
          %p This action is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
              %p
                by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,a,b) = b
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
              %p
                since if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,c) = a
                then by the previous statement
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(x,b,c) = x
                for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(b,b,c) = b
                and also
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(b,b,c) = c
          %p
            Therefore,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            (over a point).
          %p
            Conversely, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            over a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            becomes a heap, by defining
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi g
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  t(a,b,c) \,\coloneqq\, g \cdot c
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in G
            is the unique group element such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\cdot b = a
          %p
            In fact, the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heap
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the following category
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tors
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,H)
            consisting of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and a
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi H
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi,f):(G,H)\to (G',H')
            consisting of a group homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:G\to G'
            and a
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:H\to H'
          %h3#groups_as_pointed_heaps Groups as pointed heaps
          %p
            As indicated in the discussion above, a heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            acquires a group structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b) \mapsto t(a, e, b)
            as soon as an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in H
            is selected (and this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            is then the identity element of the group). Notice that every function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to H
            from a terminal set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is in fact a heap homomorphism when we consider that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            carries a unique heap structure. In different words: the free heap on a terminal set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            itself with its unique heap structure.
          %p
            It follows that the category of groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \downarrow Heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heap
            (via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prin
                  %mo :
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo →
                  %mi Heap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prin: Grp \to Heap
            and the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi Heap
                  %mo →
                  %mi Heap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: 1 \downarrow Heap \to Heap
            that forgets the point). This says that groups are equivalent to pointed heaps.
          %p
            Both of these forgetful functors are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heap
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Heap
                    %mo →
                    %mi Heap
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: 1 \downarrow Heap \to Heap
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \sqcup -
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            structure that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            carries with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocartesian+monoidal+category"} cocartesian monoidal product
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊔
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is therefore the heap
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \sqcup H
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to 1 \sqcup H
          %p
            It follows that the free group on a heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            can be constructed abstractly as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \sqcup H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            can be described as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \sqcup A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            of affine spaces are vastly easier to describe concretely than coproducts of heaps.
          %p
            Here is a more group-theoretic description of the free group on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H)
            be the structure group, given as the group of heap automorphisms of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a, b, -): H \to H
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: Str(H) \times H \to H
          %p
            denote the tautological action. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(H)
            denote the free group on the underlying set of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G, G'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo *
                  %mi G
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \ast G'
            denote their free product (coproduct). Then the free group on the heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H) \ast F(H)
            given by the coequalizer of two maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta, \gamma: F(Str(H) \times H) \rightrightarrows Str(H) \ast F(H)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is the composition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\alpha): F(Str(H) \times H) \to F(H)
            followed by the coproduct coprojection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Str
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(H) \to Str(H) \ast F(H)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is the unique group homomorphism that extends the function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo *
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H) \times H \to Str(H) \ast H
          %p
            mapping a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\theta, h)
            to their product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \cdot h
            in the group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Str
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H) \ast H
          %p
            The meaning of the construction is that group homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str(H) \ast F(H) \to G
            that factor through the coequalizer are in natural bijection with pairs
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi: Str(H) \to G, f: H \to G)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is a homomorphism and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a function, satisfying the torsor homomorphism condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\theta(h)) = \phi(\theta) \cdot f(h)
          %p
            which is an equivalent way of describing a heap homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to Prin(G)
          %h2#empty The empty heap
          %p
            If we wish
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heap
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heap
            to be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+category"} algebraic category
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-torsor"} pseudo-torsor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            becomes a heap in a unique way.
          %p
            However, in this case, some of the above theorems relating heaps to groups break down. It is of course still true that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi Heap
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp \simeq (1\downarrow Heap)
          %p
            On the other hand, we could generalize the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            to allow for an empty group. This even remains a purely algebraic notion: we can define a group as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+semigroup"} invertible semigroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\cdot,(-)^{-1})
            or an inhabited
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+quasigroup"} associative quasigroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+semigroup"} invertible semigroup
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+quasigroup"} associative quasigroup
            is a possibly-empty-heap, and every possibly-empty-heap arises in this way from its automorphism invertible semigroup or automorphism associative quasigroup (defined by either method (2) or (3)); the category of possibly-empty-heaps is equivalent to the category of invertible semigroups equipped with torsors over the point, and the category of associative quasigroups equipped with torsors over the point; etc.
          %p
            This is even
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x \in G \;|\; P\}
            is empty or inhabited iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is false or true.)
          %h2#examples_in_homotopy_theory Examples in homotopy theory
          %p
            The map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]\to[0,1]
            that sends
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\mapsto 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/3\mapsto 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2/3\mapsto 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ↦
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\mapsto 1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma X,Y]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are (unpointed) spaces,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            functor, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
            denotes the set of morphisms in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
          %p
            Thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma X,Y]
            is a (nonabelian) heap. Likewise, the full mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(\Sigma X,Y)
            can be turned into an (∞,1)-heap, defined as an (∞,1)-algebra (in spaces) over the algebraic theory of heaps.
          %p See Vokřínek  for more information.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcev+variety"} Malcev variety
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truss"} truss
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+K.+Sushkevich"}> A. K. Sushkevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theory of generalised groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%D0%90.+%D0%9A.+%D0%A1%D1%83%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87"} А. К. Сушкевич
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Теория обобщенных групп
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+T.+Johnstone"}> Peter T. Johnstone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The ‘closed subgroup theorem’ for localic herds and pregroupoids
                %strong 70
                (1991) 97-106 [
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(91)90010-y"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(91)90010-y
                ]
            %li
              %p
                G. M. Bergman, A.O. Hausknecht, Ch.IV §22 pp 95 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cogroups and co-rings in categories of associative rings
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-45"} ams:surv-45
            %li#HollingsLawson
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+D.+Hollings"}> Christopher D. Hollings
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+V.+Lawson"} Mark V. Lawson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wagner’s theory of generalised heaps
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-63621-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-63621-4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum heaps, cops and heapy categories
                %strong 12
                1 (2007) 1-9 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0701749"}> math.QA/0701749
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Thomas Booker,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Torsors, herds and flocks
                %strong 330
                (2011) 346-374 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/81154582.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.4551"} arXiv:0912.4551
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heap_%28mathematics%29"} Heap (mathematics)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/torsors.html"} Torsors made easy
                (2009)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2020/08/the_group_with_no_elements.html"} The group with no elements
                (2020)
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luk%C3%A1%C5%A1+Vok%C5%99%C3%ADnek"}> Lukáš Vokřínek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heaps and unpointed stable homotopy theory
              %strong 50
              5 (2014) 323-332 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.1709"}> arXiv:1312.1709
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.5817/AM2014-5-323"} doi:10.5817/AM2014-5-323
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/algebra"} algebra
